WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.491 --> 00:00:03.463
- [Narrator] In May, a
rare case of Monkeypox,

00:00:03.463 --> 00:00:05.760
a virus closely related to Smallpox,

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.440
was diagnosed in the UK.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.142
- That first UK case was
from a traveler in Nigeria

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:13.440
is now thought to be unconnected
to the wider outbreak,

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.620
but the UK went on quite quickly to report

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.310
many more cases.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.290
- [Narrator] Today the UK has the globe's

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.232
highest Monkeypox case numbers,

00:00:21.232 --> 00:00:24.330
and the virus has spread to more than 4500

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.581
confirmed or suspected cases across

00:00:26.581 --> 00:00:31.320
at least 40 countries,
including the US and Canada.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.440
On Tuesday, the CDC said
they're significantly

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.650
expanding Monkeypox
vaccination efforts in the US.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.960
The agency also said
it is now recommending

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.240
the vaccines for people
with presumed exposure

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.690
to the viral illness and
not just confirmed exposure.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:48.780
So, how serious is the Monkeypox outbreak?

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.610
And, should Americans be concerned

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.660
about contracting this virus?

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:57.660
Last month World Health
Organization officials

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.790
said the expected Monkeypox cases to grow

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:03.120
and stressed the
situation was containable.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.700
- This is a containable situation,

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.530
particularly in the countries like

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.270
where we are seeing these outbreaks

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.792
that are happening across Europe,

00:01:10.792 --> 00:01:14.250
in North America, as well.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.650
- [Narrator] This month the WHO said

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.840
the Monkeypox doesn't, at this point,

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.300
constitute a global health emergency.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.310
- Also, however, that they might revisit

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:27.750
that decision if the situation worsens,

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.820
for example, if there was evidence

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.040
that people were getting
more severe disease

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.020
or if there was evidence that the virus

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.210
was spreading into more vulnerable groups

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.510
like children or people with
weakened immune systems.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:42.120
- [Narrator] In the US
so far over 300 cases

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.655
have been confirmed
across at least 27 states

00:01:44.655 --> 00:01:47.190
and the District of Columbia.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:50.160
- Textbook Monkeypox typically starts

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.330
with flu-like symptoms.

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:53.430
You've got a fever, headache, muscle ache,

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.044
backache, and a few days later

00:01:55.044 --> 00:01:57.750
you get a rash normally starting

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.400
on the face and spreading out.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.840
It's a little like Chickenpox.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.110
It starts to see flat red marks

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.090
that become kind of pimple like.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.344
But, in the current outbreak

00:02:07.344 --> 00:02:08.796
there have been lots of case reports

00:02:08.796 --> 00:02:11.520
of pretty different looking symptoms.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.960
Some people are getting no rash.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.930
Some people are getting
very subtle rashes.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.401
A lot of times people are seeing

00:02:17.401 --> 00:02:20.133
a concentration of the
rash in the genital area

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:22.530
rather than starting in the face.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:24.270
- [Narrator] Scientists
believe the main way

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:27.120
Monkeypox is spread is by close contact.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.700
Previous research found
that Monkeypox virus

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.310
particles spread over short distances

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.050
via respiratory droplets,

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:35.554
but it is unknown whether Monkeypox

00:02:35.554 --> 00:02:38.024
can spread by tinier airborne particles

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.510
known as aerosols.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.490
- So there are high levels of virus

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.070
in the, like the puss filled lesions

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.960
that the disease causes

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.065
and contact with that is thought to be

00:02:49.065 --> 00:02:50.220
the main mode of spread.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.950
Monkeypox is much less easily spread

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.750
than a virus that can be spread

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.760
easily through the air like COVID-19

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.250
would be an obvious example.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.410
But, if you are in very close contact

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.110
with someone, then it
is quite easy to catch.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:05.580
- [Narrator] US health officials found

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.345
that Monkeypox cases are concentrated

00:03:07.345 --> 00:03:09.270
in specific communities.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.340
According to the CDC, at least some

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.040
of the US cases are people
who identify as gay,

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.710
bi-sexual, or men who have sex with men.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.230
- The virus can infect anyone regardless

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:22.320
of sexuality, but
infectious disease experts

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.070
think that the virus is
exposed in very close contact

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.380
between some members of
this community to spread.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:32.460
This is the first time
since the HIV epidemic

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.520
of the 1980s that a newly emerging disease

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.520
has cropped up and is
concentrated in this community.

00:03:40.642 --> 00:03:43.860
One big difference between now and then is

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.510
that while public health authorities

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:48.840
were very slow to respond
to the HIV epidemic,

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.670
this time they are making a lot of effort

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:53.654
to get the message out
to any bi-sexual men.

00:03:53.654 --> 00:03:56.310
They're doing things like
handing out information

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:57.210
at Pride events.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:59.024
They're sending push notifications

00:03:59.024 --> 00:04:01.140
on dating apps like Grinder.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.704
- [Narrator] Most cases
of Monkeypox resolve

00:04:02.704 --> 00:04:04.530
on their own without treatment.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.704
However, there are some anti-viral drugs

00:04:06.704 --> 00:04:10.170
and a vaccine that were
developed for Smallpox

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:12.750
that also work against Monkeypox.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.960
On Tuesday, Danish vaccine
maker, Bavarian Nordic,

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.090
which is the only producer of a vaccine

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:21.270
licensed for Monkeypox,
said it will meet demand.

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.454
- It's just like a traditional vaccine.

00:04:23.454 --> 00:04:25.860
It builds your immune system.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.710
It stimulates your
immune system so you are

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.996
better prepared to fight the Monkeypox

00:04:31.996 --> 00:04:34.320
you are infected with.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.940
- [Narrator] Monkeypox was discovered

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:38.760
in lab monkeys in Denmark in 1958,

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.860
hence the monkey in Monkeypox.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.450
That said, monkeys aren't thought to be

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.210
the main vector or carrier of the disease.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.820
- Scientists aren't
totally sure what species

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.980
is the main carrier, but it seems

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:52.380
to be very widely circulating among

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.772
certain rodents in the rain forests

00:04:54.772 --> 00:04:57.960
of the Congo Basin in central Africa.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.640
The first human case
was discovered in 1970

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:05.090
in a nine year old boy in the
democratic republic of Congo.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:06.360
- [Narrator] In the current outbreak

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:07.726
about four and a half thousand people

00:05:07.726 --> 00:05:10.170
have been confirmed with Monkeypox

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.900
in countries where the virus
doesn't normally occur,

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:14.430
and none of those have died.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.463
Thus far, there's only
been one death in Nigeria.

